  "body": "`crates/cl/src/cl/moves.rs` `arc_chords` uses the exact compare `ra != rb` (commit 8f99bcb4c). When it is true, the angle step also obeys `sqrt(8 * tol / hypot(r, 2|rb - ra| / d))`.\n\nFor a circular arc whose two radii differ only in the last float digits, this bound applies. It is a little smaller than the sagitta law `2 * acos(1 - tol / r)`. So the same arc can get one more chord, only because of float noise. #2483 found this in the wrapped-A golden of `microarc_test_part`.\n\nThe output is not unsafe: each chord stays inside the tolerance.\n\nDone means:\n- `arc_chords` compares the two radii with a tolerance, or the choice to keep the exact compare is recorded.\n- A unit test pins the chord count of a circle whose radii differ by float noise.\n- Goldens that change are renewed in the same PR.\n\nThis work changes posted G-code, so it is under the safety floor.",
